{"condensed":"A Vue mixin that determines which filing and administrative actions are allowed for a business entity based on its legal type, standing, user role, and feature flags.

The mixin reads business state—legal type (COOP, firm, sole proprietorship), standing, staff role—and feature flags from LaunchDarkly via `GetFeatureFlag`. The public method `isAllowed` takes an `AllowableActions` enum value and returns true or false. It routes each action through a switch statement: most actions call the private helper `isAllowedFiling`, which checks whether a filing type (and optional subtype) exists in the `getAllowedActions.filing.filingTypes` array from store state; some actions like `BUSINESS_SUMMARY` and `DETAIL_COMMENT` add additional conditions (entity type, feature flag, staff role, or the presence of a session `BUSINESS_ID`). `DIGITAL_CREDENTIALS` additionally checks `getAllowedActions.digitalBusinessCard`. No entry point shows a permission check; this mixin is called from UI to determine what to display.

GOTCHA: The default case returns `false` silently, masking unknown action values.","defines":["AllowableActionsMixin","isAllowed"],"uses":[{"name":"useBusinessStore","direction":"reads","what":"Business store providing getAllowedActions (filing types and subtypes array), getLegalType (CorpTypeCd), isEntityCoop, isEntityFirm, isEntitySoleProp, isGoodStanding getters."},{"name":"useRootStore","direction":"reads","what":"Root store providing isRoleStaff getter."},{"name":"GetFeatureFlag","direction":"sends","what":"Reads feature flags from LaunchDarkly by key (supported-dissolution-entities, special-resolution-ui-enabled, supported-business-summary-entities, supported-correction-entities, enable-digital-credentials, supported-restoration-entities, supported-put-back-on-entities)."},{"name":"AllowableActions","direction":"reads","what":"Enum defining action names (ADDRESS_CHANGE, ADMINISTRATIVE_DISSOLUTION, AGM_EXTENSION, etc.) used as switch cases."},{"name":"FilingTypes","direction":"reads","what":"Enum from bcrs-shared-components providing filing type constants (CHANGE_OF_REGISTRATION, CHANGE_OF_ADDRESS, DISSOLUTION, AGM_EXTENSION, etc.) for comparison."},{"name":"FilingSubTypes","direction":"reads","what":"Enum providing filing subtype constants (DISSOLUTION_ADMINISTRATIVE, DISSOLUTION_VOLUNTARY, FULL_RESTORATION, LIMITED_RESTORATION, LIMITED_RESTORATION_EXTENSION, LIMITED_RESTORATION_TO_FULL) for filing checks."},{"name":"CorpTypeCd","direction":"reads","what":"Enum for legal type values used in feature flag entity lists."},{"name":"AllowedActionsIF","direction":"reads","what":"Interface defining shape of allowed actions (filing array with filingTypes, digitalBusinessCard boolean)."},{"name":"sessionStorage","direction":"reads","what":"Browser sessionStorage; checks for BUSINESS_ID key to distinguish permanent from temporary business."}]}

34603.text:
{"condensed":"Utility functions for date comparison and arithmetic in YYYY-MM-DD format.

Receives two date strings (ApiDateTimeUtc) and an operator; `compareYyyyMmDd` strips hyphens, converts to numeric form, and returns the result of eval'd comparison—no input validation guards against malformed dates. `earliestYyyyMmDd` and `latestYyyyMmDd` each return the earlier or later date, handling nulls by returning the non-null date or null if both absent. `daysBetweenTwoDates` takes two Date objects, zeros their times, and returns the rounded day difference. `isDatePast` and `isDateFuture` compare a FormattedDateTimeGmt string against the current time. `addMonthsToDate` accepts a month count and YYYY-MM-DD string (length checked to 10 chars), converts to Date, adds months, and returns YYYY-MM-DD; returns null on missing input or wrong length. `subtractDates` takes two YYYY-MM-DD strings (length checked to 10), calculates month and year differences, and adjusts down by one if the day-of-month comparison suggests a month hasn't completed.

GOTCHA: `compareYyyyMmDd` uses eval() for string comparison operators, accepting any operator passed in without validation. GOTCHA: `compareYyyyMmDd` returns true on missing inputs rather than raising an error. GOTCHA: `daysBetweenTwoDates` mutates the input Date objects by calling setHours().","defines":["compareYyyyMmDd","earliestYyyyMmDd","latestYyyyMmDd","daysBetweenTwoDates","isDatePast","isDateFuture","addMonthsToDate","subtractDates"],"uses":[{"name":"isDate","direction":"sends","what":"Validation function called to check if input is a Date object; this chunk does not show what it returns."},{"name":"MS_IN_A_DAY","direction":"reads","what":"Constant defining milliseconds per day; used to convert time difference to days."},{"name":"yyyyMmDdToDate","direction":"sends","what":"Converts YYYY-MM-DD string to Date object; called by addMonthsToDate and subtractDates."},{"name":"dateToYyyyMmDd","direction":"sends","what":"Converts Date object to YYYY-MM-DD string; called by addMonthsToDate."}]}

