{"condensed":"SQLAlchemy event listeners that enforce Filing deletion restrictions and automatically set Filing status during insert and update operations.

On delete attempt: blocks deletion if `locked` or `deletion_locked` is true, raising a 403 Forbidden error with message "Deletion not allowed."

On insert or update: automatically sets `_status` based on this decision tree—skip all changes if the filing's current status is AWAITING_REVIEW, CHANGE_REQUESTED, REJECTED, or APPROVED without transaction_id, or if `skip_status_listener` flag is set; otherwise: set to EPOCH if filing_type is 'lear_epoch'; set to COMPLETED if transaction_id exists; set to PAID if payment_completion_date exists or source equals Filing.Source.COLIN; set to PENDING if payment_token exists; else set to DRAFT. This chunk shows no permission check on who invokes these listeners—SQLAlchemy fires them automatically. GOTCHA: status changes are set directly to protected `_status` field without external transaction tracking; partial state updates occur if the second listener fails after the first succeeds.","defines":["block_filing_delete_listener_function","receive_before_change"],"uses":[{"name":"Filing","direction":"receives","what":"SQLAlchemy model; before_delete, before_insert, before_update events are listened on; locked, deletion_locked, _status, filing_type, transaction_id, payment_completion_date, source, payment_token, skip_status_listener attributes are read and set"},{"name":"Filing.Status","direction":"reads","what":"Enum with values AWAITING_REVIEW, CHANGE_REQUESTED, REJECTED, APPROVED, EPOCH, COMPLETED, PAID, PENDING, DRAFT used for status comparison and assignment"},{"name":"Filing.Source.COLIN","direction":"reads","what":"Constant used to check if filing source is COLIN"},{"name":"BusinessException","direction":"sends","what":"Exception raised on delete when filing is locked or deletion_locked, with error message and 403 status"},{"name":"HTTPStatus.FORBIDDEN","direction":"reads","what":"HTTP 403 status code constant"}]}

