{"condensed":"Returns business documents (summary for all entities, certified rules and memorandum plus filing info for coops) as JSON list of document URLs and metadata, or serves the requested document as PDF or JSON.

Entry point: route GET /<identifier>/documents or /<identifier>/documents/<document_name> on blueprint. Caller must pass JWT auth via jwt.requires_auth; this chunk shows check: authorized(identifier, jwt, ['view',]) returns true or responds 401 UNAUTHORIZED. Retrieves Business by identifier; returns 404 NOT_FOUND if missing. If no document_name given, calls _get_document_list(business): builds JSON with key 'documents' holding summary URL, and for COOP legal type also calls _get_coop_documents_and_info(business) to add certifiedRules and certifiedMemorandum URLs under 'documents' and metadata under 'documentsInfo'. If document_name given, calls validate_document_request(document_name, business); if error returned, responds with error code and msg. Then serves document: if request accepts 'application/pdf', calls BusinessDocument(business, document_name).get_pdf(); if accepts 'application/json', calls BusinessDocument(business, document_name).get_json(); else 404. _get_coop_documents_and_info fetches Filing records by type 'specialResolution' filtering for rulesInResolution or memorandumInResolution flags, retrieves Document by business and type (COOP_RULES or COOP_MEMORANDUM), builds URLs and file metadata (file_key, name with filing_date formatted as legislation date, uploaded ISO timestamp), sets includedInResolution flag if matching special resolution found. Base URL read from config LEGAL_API_BASE_URL (truncated to '/api'). Metadata keys: key, name, uploaded, includedInResolution, includedInResolutionDate.

GOTCHA: no check that document_name exists or is valid before passing to BusinessDocument; validate_document_request gates this but is called only after instantiation decision.","defines":["GET /<identifier>/documents","GET /<identifier>/documents/<document_name>"],"uses":[{"name":"jwt.requires_auth","direction":"receives","what":"decorator; checked on entry to get_business_documents"},{"name":"authorized","direction":"sends","what":"called with (identifier, jwt, ['view',]) to check caller permission; returns boolean"},{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier","direction":"sends","what":"called with identifier string; returns Business or None"},{"name":"validate_document_request","direction":"sends","what":"called with (document_name, business); returns error object with msg and code, or None"},{"name":"BusinessDocument","direction":"sends","what":"instantiated with (business, document_name); get_pdf() and get_json() called to return document response"},{"name":"Filing.get_filings_by_types","direction":"sends","what":"called with (business.id, ['specialResolution']) to fetch special resolution filings"},{"name":"Document.find_by_business_id_and_type","direction":"sends","what":"called with (business.id, DocumentType.COOP_RULES.value or DocumentType.COOP_MEMORANDUM.value) to retrieve document record"},{"name":"Filing.find_by_id","direction":"sends","what":"called with filing_id to fetch filing by id"},{"name":"url_for","direction":"sends","what":"called with endpoint name and parameters to build URLs for document and filing endpoints"},{"name":"LegislationDatetime.format_as_legislation_date","direction":"sends","what":"called with filing_date to format date for display"},{"name":"current_app.config.get","direction":"reads","what":"reads LEGAL_API_BASE_URL config key"},{"name":"get_error_message","direction":"sends","what":"called with ErrorCode and identifier dict to build error response text"},{"name":"ErrorCode.NOT_AUTHORIZED","direction":"reads","what":"error code constant"},{"name":"ErrorCode.MISSING_BUSINESS","direction":"reads","what":"error code constant"},{"name":"Business.LegalTypes.COOP.value","direction":"reads","what":"legal type constant to check if business is coop"},{"name":"DocumentType.COOP_RULES.value","direction":"reads","what":"document type constant"},{"name":"DocumentType.COOP_MEMORANDUM.value","direction":"reads","what":"document type constant"}]}

37143.text:
{"condensed":"API endpoint handler for retrieving and creating comments on business filings. Provides GET and POST operations scoped to a business identifier and filing ID.

GET returns all comments for a filing, or a single comment by ID if provided. POST creates a new comment attached to a filing. Both check that the business and filing exist via `_basic_checks()`. POST additionally checks `authorized(identifier, jwt, action=['add_comment'])` and enforces that the filing ID in the JSON request body matches the URL parameter. It validates the comment payload via `validate(json_input, True)`, rejects if payload's `filingId` differs from URL `filing_id`, retrieves or creates the current user from JWT token info, then saves the comment with `comment.save()`. GET with identifier starting with 'T' loads business via `Filing.get_temp_reg_filing()` and `Business.find_by_internal_id()`, otherwise via `Business.find_by_identifier()`. The PUT, PATCH, DELETE route for versioned API calls is blocked with METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED. POST returns HTTPStatus.CREATED on success; exceptions raised by `comment.save()` return the error status code or default to CREATED/ACCEPTED. No retry, no deduplication check shown.

GOTCHA: authorization check condition `action=['add_comment']` is not shown to enforce who may perform it. GOTCHA: exception handling in POST catches `BusinessException` but swallows it; only logs via reply object. GOTCHA: `_basic_checks()` finds business differently for identifier starting 'T' but logs no explanation of this special case.","defines":["/<string:identifier>/filings/<int:filing_id>/comments (GET)","/<string:identifier>/filings/<int:filing_id>/comments/<int:comment_id> (GET)","/<string:identifier>/filings/<int:filing_id>/comments (POST)","/<string:identifier>/filings/<int:filing_id>/comments/<int:comment_id> (PUT, PATCH, DELETE)"],"uses":[{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier()","direction":"sends","what":"Query for business record by identifier string; returns Business object or None."},{"name":"Business.find_by_internal_id()","direction":"sends","what":"Query for business record by internal ID; used when identifier starts with 'T'."},{"name":"Filing.get_temp_reg_filing()","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieve temporary registration filing by identifier starting 'T'."},{"name":"Filing.find_by_id()","direction":"sends","what":"Query for filing record by filing_id; returns Filing object or None."},{"name":"Comment (model)","direction":"sends","what":"Instantiate and save Comment with staff_id, filing_id, comment text, and UTC timestamp."},{"name":"db.session.query(Comment)","direction":"sends","what":"Query comments by filing_id; may filter further by comment_id."},{"name":"User.get_or_create_user_by_jwt()","direction":"sends","what":"Retrieve or create user from JWT OIDC token info in g.jwt_oidc_token_info."},{"name":"authorized()","direction":"sends","what":"Check if caller (via identifier and jwt) is authorized for action=['add_comment']; returns boolean."},{"name":"validate()","direction":"sends","what":"Validate comment payload; returns error object with msg and code on failure, None on success."},{"name":"jwt.requires_auth","direction":"reads","what":"Decorator enforcing JWT authentication on all endpoints."},{"name":"cross_origin()","direction":"reads","what":"Flask-CORS decorator allowing requests from origin='*'."},{"name":"g.jwt_oidc_token_info","direction":"reads","what":"Flask g context variable holding OIDC token info for current request."},{"name":"request","direction":"reads","what":"Flask request object providing method, JSON body, and query parameters."}]}

