{"condensed":"Processes an incoming amalgamation application filing to create a new amalgamated business entity and records the source businesses being dissolved.

Entry point: `process(business, filing, filing_rec, filing_meta)` receives from the filing queue; this chunk shows no check that the caller may invoke it. Flow: Extracts `filing.filing.amalgamationApplication`; raises `QueueException` if missing or if business already exists. Reserves next corp number via `business_info.get_next_corp_num()`. Creates `Amalgamation` record with `filing_id`, `amalgamation_type` (from filing), `amalgamation_date` (from `filing_rec.effective_date`), and `court_approval` (boolean). Calls `create_amalgamating_businesses()` which iterates `amalgamatingBusinesses`; for each, extracts `role` and `identifier`; if `foreignJurisdiction` present, stores as `foreign_identifier`, `foreign_name`, `foreign_jurisdiction` (country uppercased), `foreign_jurisdiction_region` (if region, uppercased); else looks up local business by identifier and calls `dissolve_amalgamating_business()`. For horizontal or vertical amalgamations, locates holding or primary amalgamating business, copies its legal name, directors (via `_set_parties()` which fetches active directors, rebuilds roles with appointment date), offices (via `_set_offices()` copying registered and records offices), and share structure (via `_set_shares()` copying share classes and resolution dates). Creates new `Business` with state ACTIVE via `business_info.update_business_info()`. Updates filing with offices, parties, shares, aliases, court order. Stores `nrNumber` and `legalName` in `filing_meta.amalgamation_application`. Saves identifier, legal type, founding date to filing JSON. Returns business, filing_rec, filing_meta.

GOTCHA: `create_amalgamating_businesses()` dissolves source businesses on first call only—if a step later fails, dissolution is already recorded but business record creation may not complete.","defines":["process","create_amalgamating_businesses","dissolve_amalgamating_business","_set_parties","_set_offices","_set_shares"],"uses":[{"name":"QueueException","direction":"sends","what":"Raised when amalgamationApplication is missing from filing, business already exists, corp number unavailable, or business creation fails"},{"name":"Business.find_by_identifier","direction":"sends","what":"Looks up business by identifier to link local amalgamating business"},{"name":"Business.find_by_internal_id","direction":"sends","what":"Looks up primary or holding business to copy its legal name, directors, offices, shares"},{"name":"Business.State.HISTORICAL","direction":"reads","what":"State constant set on dissolved amalgamating businesses"},{"name":"Business.State.ACTIVE","direction":"reads","what":"State constant set on newly created amalgamated business"},{"name":"Amalgamation","direction":"sends","what":"Created and linked to new business, stores filing_id, type, date, court_approval flag"},{"name":"AmalgamatingBusiness","direction":"sends","what":"Created for each source business with role, business_id or foreign identifiers"},{"name":"AmalgamatingBusiness.Role.holding","direction":"reads","what":"Role constant to identify holding business in horizontal/vertical amalgamations"},{"name":"AmalgamatingBusiness.Role.primary","direction":"reads","what":"Role constant to identify primary business in horizontal/vertical amalgamations"},{"name":"Amalgamation.AmalgamationTypes.horizontal","direction":"reads","what":"Type constant to determine if source business attributes are copied"},{"name":"Amalgamation.AmalgamationTypes.vertical","direction":"reads","what":"Type constant to determine if source business attributes are copied"},{"name":"PartyRole.get_active_directors","direction":"sends","what":"Fetches active directors of holding/primary business as of filing effective date"},{"name":"PartyRole.RoleTypes.COMPLETING_PARTY","direction":"reads","what":"Role type value to identify completing party from filing parties"},{"name":"JSON_ROLE_CONVERTER","direction":"reads","what":"Maps roleType strings to PartyRole.RoleTypes values"},{"name":"OfficeType.REGISTERED","direction":"reads","what":"Office type constant to filter offices copied from source business"},{"name":"OfficeType.RECORDS","direction":"reads","what":"Office type constant to filter offices copied from source business"},{"name":"db.session.add","direction":"sends","what":"Stages dissolved business for commit"},{"name":"business_info.get_next_corp_num","direction":"sends","what":"Reserves next available corp number for legalType"},{"name":"business_info.update_business_info","direction":"sends","what":"Populates business with corp_num, legal name, NR number, legal type, founding date from business_info_obj"},{"name":"update_offices","direction":"sends","what":"Updates new business offices from filing offices"},{"name":"update_parties","direction":"sends","what":"Updates new business parties from filing parties"},{"name":"shares.update_share_structure","direction":"sends","what":"Updates new business share structure from filing shareStructure"},{"name":"aliases.update_aliases","direction":"sends","what":"Updates new business aliases from filing nameTranslations"},{"name":"filings.update_filing_court_order","direction":"sends","what":"Updates filing record with court order details"}]}

38733.text:
{"condensed":"Processes change-of-directors filings by applying director appointment, modification, and cessation actions to a business model. Entry point is `process(business, filing, filing_meta)`, callable by any filer workflow with no check shown.

Reads `filing['changeOfDirectors']['directors']` array; for each director, checks if it came from colin via `filing.get('colinIds')`. If so, matches the new director against existing `PartyRole` directors by name (case-insensitive) to determine action: if name matches an active director with no cessation date, action is 'modified'; if name matches a ceased director but new record has no cessation date, action is 'appointed'; if no match, action is 'appointed'; if matched director is cease-dated and new record has cessation date, action is 'ceased'. For action 'appointed', calls `create_party(business_id, party_info)` and `create_role(party, role_info)` to insert new director party role into `business.party_roles`. For actions 'modified', 'ceased', or other non-appointment actions, resolves the director name (using `prevFirstName`, `prevMiddleInitial`, `prevLastName` if action is 'nameChanged'), matches against active directors, and calls `update_director(director, new_info)`. After processing all new directors from colin, ceases any existing active director not in the new list by setting `cessation_date` to `datetime.utcnow()`. Sets `business.last_cod_date` to `filing_meta.application_date`.

Raises `QueueException` if director name cannot be resolved from filing. This chunk shows no permission check. GOTCHA: name comparison concatenates fields without checking for None; middle_initial defaulting to empty string masks that. GOTCHA: for colin filings, active directors absent from new list are auto-ceased without an explicit 'ceased' action in the filing.","defines":["process"],"uses":[{"name":"datetime.utcnow","direction":"sends","what":"Current UTC timestamp, called to set cessation_date when ceasing directors."},{"name":"QueueException","direction":"sends","what":"Raised when director name cannot be resolved from filing."},{"name":"logger.error","direction":"sends","what":"Logs error message when director name resolution fails."},{"name":"create_party","direction":"sends","what":"Creates new party with business_id and party_info (officer details); used for appointed directors."},{"name":"create_role","direction":"sends","what":"Creates new director role attached to a party with roleType, appointmentDate, and cessationDate."},{"name":"update_director","direction":"sends","what":"Updates existing director record with new_info from filing."},{"name":"Business.last_cod_date","direction":"sends","what":"Field set to filing_meta.application_date when processing begins."},{"name":"Business.party_roles","direction":"sends","what":"List appended with new director roles when action is 'appointed'."},{"name":"PartyRole.get_parties_by_role","direction":"reads","what":"Queries existing directors for a business by business.id and PartyRole.RoleTypes.DIRECTOR.value role type; returns party roles including party.first_name, party.middle_initial, party.last_name, and cessation_date."},{"name":"PartyRole.RoleTypes.DIRECTOR","direction":"reads","what":"Constant role type value used to filter director queries."},{"name":"filing['changeOfDirectors']['directors']","direction":"reads","what":"Array of new director objects with officer (firstName, middleInitial, lastName, prevFirstName, prevMiddleInitial, prevLastName), appointmentDate, cessationDate, and actions fields."},{"name":"filing.get('colinIds')","direction":"reads","what":"Optional identifier indicating filing originated from colin system; when present triggers special matching and auto-cease logic."}]}

38736.text:
{"condensed":"Processes a consent continuation out filing by extracting court order, foreign jurisdiction details, and expiry date from the filing JSON, then populates a ConsentContinuationOut database record linked to the business and updates filing metadata.

Caller: Entry point `process(business, cco_filing, filing, filing_meta)` called by entity_filer framework to render consent continuation out filing into business model; this chunk shows no check. Extracts from filing JSON: `/consentContinuationOut/courtOrder` passed to `update_filing_court_order()`, with IndexError/KeyError/TypeError silently suppressed. Reads `foreignJurisdiction.country` (uppercased) and `foreignJurisdiction.region` (uppercased if present, else None). Calls `get_expiry_date(cco_filing)` to compute expiry 6 months after filing effective_date, handling daylight saving time offset drift by converting effective_date and computed date to legislation timezone, calculating DST difference, and applying correction before converting to UTC. Creates ConsentContinuationOut with foreign_jurisdiction, foreign_jurisdiction_region, expiry_date, filing_id, business_id; appends to business.consent_continuation_outs. Sets filing_meta.consent_continuation_out to dict holding 'country', 'region' (both strings), 'expiry' (ISO format string).

GOTCHA: Court order update exception is silently suppressed with `suppress(IndexError, KeyError, TypeError)` — failures are not logged or recorded.","defines":["process","get_expiry_date"],"uses":[{"name":"filings.update_filing_court_order","direction":"sends","what":"Receives cco_filing and court order JSON from filing path /consentContinuationOut/courtOrder; updates filing record"},{"name":"ConsentContinuationOut","direction":"receives","what":"Instantiated and populated with foreign jurisdiction, expiry date, and IDs; appended to business model"},{"name":"LegislationDatetime.as_legislation_timezone","direction":"sends","what":"Receives datetime to convert to legislation timezone; called twice in expiry calculation"},{"name":"LegislationDatetime.as_utc_timezone","direction":"sends","what":"Receives datetime with DST adjustment applied; converts to UTC for final expiry_date"},{"name":"datedelta.datedelta","direction":"sends","what":"Receives months=6 to add 6 months to effective_date"},{"name":"Business.consent_continuation_outs","direction":"sends","what":"Appends new ConsentContinuationOut record to business collection"},{"name":"Filing.effective_date","direction":"reads","what":"Reads filing effective_date to calculate expiry 6 months forward"},{"name":"FilingMeta","direction":"sends","what":"Updates consent_continuation_out dict with country, region, and expiry ISO string"}]}

38747.text:
{"condensed":"Applies a correction filing to the Business record, updating legal name, cooperative association type, nature of business, name translations, offices, parties, court order, start date, share structure, resolution, signatory, signing date, resolution date, rules, and memorandum. Tracks what-changed pairs in filing_meta.correction.

