{"condensed":"Audit base class for ORM models to track creation and modification metadata in the pay-api database system.

This abstract SQLAlchemy base class automatically adds four audit columns to any model that inherits from it: `created_on` (timestamps at UTC on insert), `updated_on` (timestamps at UTC on each update), `created_by` (populated by calling `_get_user_name` at insert, stores up to 50 chars), and `updated_by` (populated at update, nullable, up to 50 chars). It also adds `created_name` and `updated_name` (up to 100 and 50 chars respectively, nullable, via `_get_name`). Both `_get_user_name` and `_get_name` are decorated with `@user_context` and extract values from `kwargs['user'].user_name` and `kwargs['user'].name`. `AuditSchema` defines marshmallow serialization for `created_on` and `updated_on` fields only.

